WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.887
You type job. The record on screen

00:00:02.907 --> 00:00:05.657
contains jobs. Can an ordinary lexical

00:00:05.677 --> 00:00:06.881
search match them?

00:00:07.043 --> 00:00:09.163
If it can, does that mean the system used

00:00:09.183 --> 00:00:10.335
semantic search?

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:11.391
Take a moment.

00:00:13.804 --> 00:00:16.032
It can match when text analysis brings the

00:00:16.052 --> 00:00:18.853
forms to a compatible indexed term.

00:00:19.016 --> 00:00:21.212
That does not require dense retrieval.

00:00:21.387 --> 00:00:23.184
The important comparison is between the

00:00:23.204 --> 00:00:25.826
processed terms, not just the visible

00:00:25.846 --> 00:00:26.908
spellings.

00:00:27.824 --> 00:00:30.355
Follow the chapter's sample: Delulu about

00:00:30.375 --> 00:00:33.190
jobs, followed by an exclamation mark.

00:00:33.365 --> 00:00:35.459
Its illustrative tokenizer makes four

00:00:35.479 --> 00:00:38.667
units: Delulu, about, jobs, and the

00:00:38.687 --> 00:00:41.231
punctuation. Each unit is a token.

00:00:41.813 --> 00:00:43.954
Tokens are not always whole words.

00:00:44.142 --> 00:00:46.699
They can be punctuation, parts of words,

00:00:46.719 --> 00:00:48.915
characters or other units.

00:00:49.078 --> 00:00:52.047
Names, hyphens, identifiers and languages

00:00:52.067 --> 00:00:53.723
with different boundary conventions

00:00:53.743 --> 00:00:55.088
require choices.

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:57.821
Tokenisation divides the string; it is

00:00:57.841 --> 00:01:00.616
only one step in text analysis.

00:01:01.533 --> 00:01:03.990
In this example, case normalisation

00:01:04.010 --> 00:01:05.652
lowercases Delulu.

00:01:05.815 --> 00:01:07.895
Optional removal drops about and the

00:01:07.915 --> 00:01:09.222
exclamation mark.

00:01:09.384 --> 00:01:12.186
Optional stemming changes jobs to job.

00:01:12.374 --> 00:01:14.583
The final indexed terms are delulu and

00:01:14.603 --> 00:01:15.291
job.

00:01:15.883 --> 00:01:18.189
These are separate operations, not a

00:01:18.209 --> 00:01:19.593
universal recipe.

00:01:19.768 --> 00:01:22.171
Another analyser might retain about,

00:01:22.191 --> 00:01:25.264
preserve jobs or keep an entire value in a

00:01:25.284 --> 00:01:27.815
keyword field. Never assume every

00:01:27.835 --> 00:01:30.521
displayed word becomes a searchable term.

00:01:31.437 --> 00:01:33.862
Stemming uses rules or heuristics to

00:01:33.882 --> 00:01:36.852
reduce forms. Studies, studying and

00:01:36.872 --> 00:01:38.681
studied might become studi.

00:01:38.856 --> 00:01:41.233
That matching key need not be a dictionary

00:01:41.253 --> 00:01:44.236
word. Lemmatisation uses vocabulary and

00:01:44.256 --> 00:01:47.328
morphology to choose a dictionary form,

00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:48.423
such as study.

00:01:49.004 --> 00:01:52.132
Grammar still matters: adjectival better

00:01:52.152 --> 00:01:53.292
may become good.

00:01:53.467 --> 00:01:55.483
These outputs are illustrative, not

00:01:55.503 --> 00:01:57.892
guaranteed. Different algorithms,

00:01:58.029 --> 00:02:00.457
languages, dictionaries and fields can

00:02:00.477 --> 00:02:02.880
behave differently, or apply neither

00:02:02.900 --> 00:02:03.884
process.

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:07.567
When related grammatical forms meet at one

00:02:07.587 --> 00:02:10.698
term, useful matches can become possible.

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:13.186
Over-stemming can also collapse unrelated

00:02:13.206 --> 00:02:15.260
words and lose precision.

00:02:15.422 --> 00:02:17.193
Under-stemming leaves related forms

00:02:17.213 --> 00:02:19.847
separate and can miss a useful match.

00:02:20.417 --> 00:02:22.740
An incorrect grammatical interpretation

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:24.865
can also harm lemmatisation.

00:02:25.028 --> 00:02:27.804
Neither method is synonym expansion,

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:29.918
controlled-vocabulary mapping or a

00:02:29.938 --> 00:02:31.141
guarantee of meaning.

00:02:31.316 --> 00:02:33.448
Test the analysis on the collection and

00:02:33.468 --> 00:02:35.497
fields you actually search.

00:02:36.405 --> 00:02:38.946
On the document side, jobs may be stored

00:02:38.966 --> 00:02:40.299
as indexed job.

00:02:40.448 --> 00:02:43.598
On the query side, job may remain job.

00:02:43.773 --> 00:02:46.124
Both sides consult the same dictionary

00:02:46.144 --> 00:02:49.024
entry, so the document can match despite

00:02:49.044 --> 00:02:50.492
the different surface form.

00:02:51.056 --> 00:02:53.291
Now let the index store only jobs while

00:02:53.311 --> 00:02:55.791
the query looks up only job.

00:02:55.966 --> 00:02:58.137
Without another mapping, that document is

00:02:58.157 --> 00:03:01.383
missed. No error message is required.

00:03:01.559 --> 00:03:03.987
Query and document analysis need to be

00:03:04.007 --> 00:03:06.887
compatible, even when their operations are

00:03:06.907 --> 00:03:08.175
not identical.

00:03:09.083 --> 00:03:11.480
User-entered truncation, such as librar

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:14.160
star, is separate from stemming and

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:16.738
lemmatisation. Its expansion depends on

00:03:16.758 --> 00:03:19.868
platform syntax and indexed forms.

00:03:20.018 --> 00:03:22.575
If related words unexpectedly fail to

00:03:22.595 --> 00:03:26.093
match, inspect that analysis and expansion

00:03:26.113 --> 00:03:28.309
before blaming AND or OR.

00:03:28.889 --> 00:03:30.067
Fields can differ too.

00:03:30.229 --> 00:03:32.735
A title-and-abstract field might reduce

00:03:32.755 --> 00:03:35.879
grammatical forms, while a code, exact

00:03:35.899 --> 00:03:38.470
name or identifier deliberately preserves

00:03:38.490 --> 00:03:39.783
the original value.

00:03:39.946 --> 00:03:42.825
Ask what was indexed, how it was analysed,

00:03:42.845 --> 00:03:44.655
and what the query actually looked up.
